Expanding the squared norm, we have:
\begin{align\*}
\loss\_1 &= \frac{1}{n} \mathbf{a}^T(I - \frac{2\eta}{n}XX^\top)^T(I - \frac{2\eta}{n}XX^\top)\mathbf{a} \
&= \frac{1}{n} \mathbf{a}^T(I^T - \frac{2\eta}{n}X^\top X)(I - \frac{2\eta}{n}XX^\top)\mathbf{a} \
&= \frac{1}{n} \mathbf{a}^T I^T I \mathbf{a} - \frac{2\eta}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X I \mathbf{a} + \frac{\eta^2}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X X^\top X \mathbf{a} \
&= \frac{1}{n} \mathbf{a}^T \mathbf{a} - \frac{2\eta}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X \mathbf{a} + \frac{\eta^2}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X X^\top X \mathbf{a}.
\end{align\*}
Taking the derivative with respect to $\eta$, we have:
\begin{align\*}
\frac{d \loss\_1}{d \eta} &= -\frac{2}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X \mathbf{a} + \frac{2\eta}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X X^\top X \mathbf{a} \
&= \frac{2}{n^2} \eta \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X X^\top X \mathbf{a} - \frac{2}{n^2} \mathbf{a}^T X^\top X \mathbf{a}.
\end{align\*}
The memory complexity of computing this gradient is $\mathcal{O}(dn)$ as we need to store $\mathbf{a}$, $X$ and $X^\top X$.

